  "question": {
    "text": "Imagine that a reactor converts all the given mass into energy and that it operates at a power level of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Watt</mi></math> . The mass of the fuel consumed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>per</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>hour</mi></math>, in the reactor, will be:<br />(velocity of light,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8&#160;</mn></msup><mn>m</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>s</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
